# KNOWN GAP (filed 2026-08-15 from the R42 Track-D brief-review pass 11,
# orchestrator-verified): the compiler's INTERNAL postcondition alias
# `__return__` is spellable in ORDINARY user source — `int x = __return__`
# passes `gg check`, builds, and prints 0 (the resolve-side guard for the
# postcondition rewrite shields the name globally). A user identifier that
# silently binds a compiler-internal slot is a reserved-name leak.
# INTENDED: check-time reject (undefined name / reserved identifier) —
# an accept->reject change that binds Core #9's all-lanes obligation
# (three self-host parser copies + self-host resolve mirror the
# convention), so it lands as its own cross-lane track, not a rider.
# Wired test: user_spelled_dunder_return_rejected (tests/integration.rs, #[ignore]d).
void main():
    int x = __return__
    print(x)
